(Regression test: format-string parts must resolve identically in every
 sink. Name resolution lives in one shared resolve_format_variable -
 previously Print supported special names like {arguments's name} that
 the buffer set/copy/append sinks silently dropped.)

a number called "v" is 255.

Print "print: {v} {v:04x} {v:b} {v:o}".

Create a buffer called buf.
copy "buffer: {v} {v:04x} {v:b} {v:o}" to buf.
Print buf.

Open a file at 1 for writing called out.
write "write: {v} {v:04x} {v:b} {v:o}\n" to out.

(special name in a buffer sink - previously Print-only)
Create a buffer called argbuf.
copy "count via buffer: {arguments's count}" to argbuf.
Print argbuf.
